! **A non-magnetic hydrogen chain, whose Fermi surface is two points.**
!
! The same cell as `h-chain-spiral.in` -- one hydrogen every 5 bohr along z,
! 12 bohr from its images in x and y -- but unpolarized, because that is the
! state whose instability the nesting function is about. A spiral grows out of
! the paramagnet, so `N(q)` is computed on the paramagnet and its peak is the
! pitch the spiral is predicted to choose; `relax_spiral_q` then goes and finds
! it (P21: 0.50003).
!
! One electron per cell in a spin-degenerate band is **half filling**, so
! `k_F = pi/2c` and the only wavevector that connects the two Fermi points is
! `2 k_F = pi/c`, which is `q = 0.5` in crystal coordinates. That is an
! analytic answer with no reference output behind it, which is the point of the
! case.
!
! `1 1 n` k-grids throughout: the transverse dispersion at 12 bohr separation is
! numerically zero and sampling it would only dilute the one-dimensional Fermi
! surface being resolved.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 0.41666666666667,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.02
    nbnd = 6
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 16 0 0 0
